01:04:14.409 --> 01:04:18.331
and to create bigger distance
between somebody copying you,

01:04:18.331 --> 01:04:22.102
that's meaningful, and
you don't give up control,

01:04:22.102 --> 01:04:24.779
it's a worthwhile debate.

01:04:24.779 --> 01:04:28.276
80% of 100 million's better
than 100% of 40 million

01:04:28.276 --> 01:04:30.359
from a dollar standpoint.

01:04:31.368 --> 01:04:34.870
Just don't think that
just 'cause you sold off

01:04:34.870 --> 01:04:37.863
20% of your company doesn't mean

01:04:37.863 --> 01:04:40.181
that you're not gonna be held accountable.

01:04:40.181 --> 01:04:41.534
Let me give you an example.

01:04:41.534 --> 01:04:45.463
When AJ and I sold a piece of
VaynerMedia to Stephen Ross,

01:04:45.463 --> 01:04:47.530
one of the things that I made required

01:04:47.530 --> 01:04:48.951
is that I never had to have a meeting

01:04:48.951 --> 01:04:50.881
to tell them how the business was doing.

01:04:50.881 --> 01:04:52.521
- [Woman] Alright.

01:04:52.521 --> 01:04:53.641
- You like that?

01:04:53.641 --> 01:04:54.474
- [Audience] Yeah!

01:04:54.474 --> 01:04:55.849
- It's a good one, right?

01:04:55.849 --> 01:04:58.394
Now, he was worth eight billion dollars,

01:04:58.394 --> 01:04:59.476
so he could give a crap ass.

01:04:59.476 --> 01:05:03.151
You need to make sure,
whether you sell 1%,

01:05:03.151 --> 01:05:05.384
you could sell 1% of your company,

01:05:05.384 --> 01:05:06.978
and that investor might take up

01:05:06.978 --> 01:05:09.988
a disproportionate amount of your time.

01:05:09.988 --> 01:05:12.047
The biggest issue is time

01:05:12.047 --> 01:05:14.327
when you sell a piece of your company.

01:05:14.327 --> 01:05:16.901
Do you really wanna
prep for an entire week

01:05:16.901 --> 01:05:19.403
every 90 days for an investor meeting

01:05:19.403 --> 01:05:21.635
so you can justify your behavior?

01:05:21.635 --> 01:05:23.476
- [Woman] Yeah, but the thing is,

01:05:23.476 --> 01:05:27.278
I'm quite keen on taking that offer,

01:05:27.278 --> 01:05:30.505
because it's much more
of a strategy partnership

01:05:30.505 --> 01:05:33.160
that will bring up value to me.

01:05:33.160 --> 01:05:34.412
- So let's talk about that for a minute.

01:05:34.412 --> 01:05:37.011
Is it a human or is it a company?

01:05:37.011 --> 01:05:38.261
- [Woman] Both.

01:05:39.478 --> 01:05:42.030
Because, it's a company, yeah.

01:05:42.030 --> 01:05:44.448
- Is the human that you're excited about

01:05:44.448 --> 01:05:47.977
being a strategic value
prop to you an employee

01:05:47.977 --> 01:05:49.965
of the company or owns the company?

01:05:49.965 --> 01:05:51.014
- [Woman] Owns the company.

01:05:51.014 --> 01:05:51.977
- Okay.

01:05:51.977 --> 01:05:54.455
So you feel you'll get
value from this individual?

01:05:54.455 --> 01:05:55.607
- [Woman] Yeah, both sides,

01:05:55.607 --> 01:05:58.310
because they wanted to
invest because they wanted

01:05:58.310 --> 01:06:01.714
to have us under their property as well.

01:06:01.714 --> 01:06:03.248
- Sure.
- 'Cause that could bring

01:06:03.248 --> 01:06:04.578
certain value to them, as well,

01:06:04.578 --> 01:06:06.135
so that's why they want it, so.

01:06:06.135 --> 01:06:07.067
- Of course.
- Yeah.

01:06:07.067 --> 01:06:08.550
- How, I mean, you know,

01:06:08.550 --> 01:06:10.093
as you can see, as we're digging,

01:06:10.093 --> 01:06:11.918
there's no right answer to this question.

01:06:11.918 --> 01:06:13.575
- [Woman] Yeah, there's
no right at all, yeah.

01:06:13.575 --> 01:06:14.826
- I think the question
becomes how comfortable

01:06:14.826 --> 01:06:16.166
you feel with them.

01:06:16.166 --> 01:06:20.646
I think you need to make sure
you over talk expectations.

01:06:20.646 --> 01:06:22.846
Young entrepreneurs often make the mistake

01:06:22.846 --> 01:06:26.679
of only seeing the good
side of an investment.

01:06:27.747 --> 01:06:29.731
And there's, nobody's giving you lots

01:06:29.731 --> 01:06:33.231
of money 'cause they think you're awesome.

01:06:34.239 --> 01:06:36.209
And so, you just need to be thoughtful.

01:06:36.209 --> 01:06:38.142
The amount of people that
I've seen raise capital

01:06:38.142 --> 01:06:41.390
when they didn't need to and
it destroyed their business,

01:06:41.390 --> 01:06:44.531
is more than I'd like to say.

01:06:44.531 --> 01:06:46.822
At the same token,

01:06:46.822 --> 01:06:48.907
there's a ton of people
who would have failed

01:06:48.907 --> 01:06:51.687
and gone out of business
without a strategic investment,

01:06:51.687 --> 01:06:53.873
and then it turned into a huge success.

01:06:53.873 --> 01:06:55.517
Here's what I would say.

01:06:55.517 --> 01:06:57.348
Everything that's in your stomach

01:06:57.348 --> 01:06:59.621
that you wanna ask and talk about,

01:06:59.621 --> 01:07:01.712
do it before you sign that contract.

01:07:01.712 --> 01:07:03.774
That's the mistake.

01:07:03.774 --> 01:07:05.570
You sit on two or three
things that you just

01:07:05.570 --> 01:07:07.856
think will work themselves out,

01:07:07.856 --> 01:07:09.565
bring them to the forefront.

01:07:09.565 --> 01:07:11.857
- Okay.
- Make sense?

01:07:11.857 --> 01:07:13.514
- Yeah, it makes sense.
- I'm sure there's one

01:07:13.514 --> 01:07:15.299
to two things that are in your head.

01:07:15.299 --> 01:07:16.450
- [Woman] Yeah, a few things,

01:07:16.450 --> 01:07:17.874
like you were saying
there's no right or wrong,

01:07:17.874 --> 01:07:20.221
it's just, I have a certain angle

01:07:20.221 --> 01:07:22.496
that I wanted to get to, and.

01:07:22.496 --> 01:07:25.143
- What does angle mean?

01:07:25.143 --> 01:07:26.298
Dollar amount?

01:07:26.298 --> 01:07:27.381
- [Woman] No, no, no.

01:07:27.381 --> 01:07:30.458
It's in, itself, the impact of the company

01:07:30.458 --> 01:07:33.857
that I wanted to, because
the kind of impact I wanted

01:07:33.857 --> 01:07:37.125
to get, I wanted to have
that certain impact,

01:07:37.125 --> 01:07:41.159
the level that I wanted to
have it, I need a partner.

01:07:41.159 --> 01:07:42.699
And that's what.

01:07:42.699 --> 01:07:44.567
- Can I ask you a question?
- Yeah.

01:07:44.567 --> 01:07:47.490
- The impact that you
want the company to have,

01:07:47.490 --> 01:07:51.407
could you get to that
impact 11 years from now?

01:07:52.488 --> 01:07:54.097
- [Woman] Yeah.

01:07:54.097 --> 01:07:56.015
- So, then you have to ask yourself,

01:07:56.015 --> 01:07:59.356
are you trying to get
to the impact sooner,

01:07:59.356 --> 01:08:01.345
and you're putting that as a romantic

01:08:01.345 --> 01:08:03.128
point of view in your head,

01:08:03.128 --> 01:08:07.090
and are you giving up too
much to get there sooner,

01:08:07.090 --> 01:08:10.371
because it's just one
bigger version of patience,

01:08:10.371 --> 01:08:13.833
this is why I'm pounding
patience down people's throats.

01:08:13.833 --> 01:08:17.014
And more importantly, is this impact real,

01:08:17.014 --> 01:08:19.972
or is it manifested in your
head as a romantic thing,

01:08:19.972 --> 01:08:21.585
you know, you gotta
think about those things.

01:08:21.585 --> 01:08:23.344
- [Woman] No, it's real,
because the thing is,

01:08:23.344 --> 01:08:27.893
with our company, we're
super engaged, because,

01:08:27.893 --> 01:08:31.104
customers and our followers,
they don't see us as brands,

01:08:31.104 --> 01:08:33.508
they see us as a friend.

01:08:33.508 --> 01:08:35.886
So, that's how we built, like.

01:08:35.886 --> 01:08:38.073
- Be careful, because, at scale,

01:08:38.073 --> 01:08:40.304
that tends to go away.
- Yeah, I get that, yeah.

01:08:40.304 --> 01:08:41.211
That's the thing,

01:08:41.211 --> 01:08:44.910
we have to have a
certain balance somewhat,

01:08:44.910 --> 01:08:46.006
yeah, as we scale.

01:08:46.006 --> 01:08:49.274
- That was probably the thing
that scared me the most,

01:08:49.274 --> 01:08:50.107
because,

01:08:51.348 --> 01:08:54.166
if that's how your consumers feel,

01:08:54.166 --> 01:08:58.273
it's almost impossible for
somebody investing in you

01:08:58.273 --> 01:09:01.424
to being comfortable with
you doing the behavior

01:09:01.424 --> 01:09:03.973
that makes that 100% pure.

01:09:03.973 --> 01:09:06.958
They are thinking about the scale of that,

01:09:06.958 --> 01:09:10.712
which then dilutes the energy of that.

01:09:10.712 --> 01:09:13.014
- [Woman] It's not my voice,
it's the company's voice.

01:09:13.014 --> 01:09:15.856
So, they don't see the brand as a person,

01:09:15.856 --> 01:09:17.246
it's just, they feel like--
- I understand.

01:09:17.246 --> 01:09:18.338
- Yeah, yeah.
- I understand.

01:09:18.338 --> 01:09:19.796
- [Woman] When they see the, like,

01:09:19.796 --> 01:09:21.638
the people that runs this
company has a certain value

01:09:21.638 --> 01:09:24.064
that they resonate to, so, yeah.

01:09:24.064 --> 01:09:25.855
- Let me ask one last
question, and we'll move on.

01:09:25.855 --> 01:09:28.864
Does the investor have any
say after the transaction?

01:09:28.864 --> 01:09:30.335
- [Woman] No, not really.

01:09:30.335 --> 01:09:31.556
- Good, then do it.

01:09:31.556 --> 01:09:32.752
- [Woman] Yeah, alright.

01:09:32.752 --> 01:09:33.700
(audience laughing)

01:09:33.700 --> 01:09:36.655
- But just make sure you
define the not really part.

01:09:36.655 --> 01:09:37.731
- [Woman] Yeah, because, no,

01:09:37.731 --> 01:09:39.765
because they do have a certain,

01:09:39.765 --> 01:09:42.750
they, based on the
conversations that we have,

01:09:42.750 --> 01:09:45.681
they do wanted to offer advice,

01:09:45.681 --> 01:09:49.683
try to bring up a certain value for us,

01:09:49.683 --> 01:09:52.231
but, Gary Vee, ultimately,
it's still my decision,

01:09:52.231 --> 01:09:54.204
'cause that's what they, they told.

01:09:54.204 --> 01:09:55.445
- Ownership.
- Yeah.

01:09:55.445 --> 01:09:56.416
- Good luck.
- Thank you so much.

01:09:56.416 --> 01:09:57.833
- You're welcome.

01:10:06.001 --> 01:10:07.184
Did we lose it?

01:10:07.184 --> 01:10:08.941
There we go.

01:10:08.941 --> 01:10:09.837
- [Shawn] Hi, Gary.

01:10:09.837 --> 01:10:10.670
- How are you?

01:10:10.670 --> 01:10:12.367
- [Shawn] I'm good,
I'm good, and yourself?

01:10:12.367 --> 01:10:17.308
Okay, I'm Shawn, I'm a digital
marketer from Malaysia.

01:10:17.308 --> 01:10:19.334
First off, I took your advice,

01:10:19.334 --> 01:10:21.179
and I started vlogging not too long ago,

01:10:21.179 --> 01:10:23.701
and I'm already seeing work,

01:10:23.701 --> 01:10:25.527
doors that I could never
imagine are starting

01:10:25.527 --> 01:10:28.390
to open for me, and I only
have you to thank you for that.

01:10:28.390 --> 01:10:30.291
I have a two part question,

01:10:30.291 --> 01:10:32.826
first, my father owns a
traditional billboard business

01:10:32.826 --> 01:10:35.588
with about 1,000 sites,
mostly along the highway.

01:10:35.588 --> 01:10:38.368
I'm persuading him to
invest into it digitally,

01:10:38.368 --> 01:10:40.366
I don't work for his business yet,

01:10:40.366 --> 01:10:42.184
but I assume I will in the future.

01:10:42.184 --> 01:10:43.624
Given your expertise,

01:10:43.624 --> 01:10:45.811
if we became partners
today in this business,

01:10:45.811 --> 01:10:47.438
how would you focus your resources,

01:10:47.438 --> 01:10:50.174
and what would you, what
would your first steps be?

01:10:50.174 --> 01:10:51.441
- What kind of business is it?

01:10:51.441 --> 01:10:54.113
- [Shawn] A traditional
billboard business.

01:10:54.113 --> 01:10:55.775
- Traditional what?
- Billboard.

01:10:55.775 --> 01:10:57.358
- Billboard.
- Yeah.

01:10:59.331 --> 01:11:01.387
- So, your dad owns billboards.

01:11:01.387 --> 01:11:04.398
- [Shawn] Yes, 1,000
sites along the highway.

01:11:04.398 --> 01:11:06.829
- Which is rad, is it, are they digital?

01:11:06.829 --> 01:11:07.905
- [Shawn] No.

01:11:07.905 --> 01:11:09.293
It's too early.
- So,

01:11:09.293 --> 01:11:11.476
I would probably make the capital invest,

01:11:11.476 --> 01:11:14.549
if I took over my dad's
business or became his partner,

01:11:14.549 --> 01:11:17.671
I'd probably take the
capital risk up front

01:11:17.671 --> 01:11:19.554
to take them digital,

01:11:19.554 --> 01:11:22.003
'cause I think that's gonna be required

01:11:22.003 --> 01:11:25.662
to get the value out of that outdoor.

01:11:25.662 --> 01:11:28.245
I would also look to diversify,

01:11:30.122 --> 01:11:32.890
'cause I'd be too fearful,
you're a young dude,

01:11:32.890 --> 01:11:35.521
I'm too fearful about self-driving cars

01:11:35.521 --> 01:11:36.975
and all the things that
happen over the next

01:11:36.975 --> 01:11:39.787
20, 30 years that would disproportionately

01:11:39.787 --> 01:11:43.620
decrease the value of
the asset that you have.

01:11:44.578 --> 01:11:47.459
So, my intuition is
that I would diversify,

01:11:47.459 --> 01:11:50.237
I would either sell off half the boards

01:11:50.237 --> 01:11:52.781
and then put it into
building a media company,

01:11:52.781 --> 01:11:55.608
or I would reinvest all
the profits each year

01:11:55.608 --> 01:11:58.404
into building some sort
of digital complement

01:11:58.404 --> 01:12:00.948
to a traditional product like that.

01:12:00.948 --> 01:12:02.418
- [Shawn] Okay, got it.

01:12:02.418 --> 01:12:03.944
The second part to the question is

01:12:03.944 --> 01:12:06.205
as an extension to my vlogging,

01:12:06.205 --> 01:12:08.820
I plan to start a series
of interview videos

01:12:08.820 --> 01:12:11.559
of podcast sessions with
people within the same field

01:12:11.559 --> 01:12:13.904
to talk about what they do,

01:12:13.904 --> 01:12:16.979
and I was wondering, this
is, starting my luck here,

01:12:16.979 --> 01:12:19.954
would be my first guest to officiate this?

01:12:19.954 --> 01:12:21.993
- So, I won't, but.

01:12:21.993 --> 01:12:23.558
- [Shawn] Ouch, see, that hurts.

01:12:23.558 --> 01:12:27.314
- But, if you do 15
episodes, I'll be your 16th.

01:12:27.314 --> 01:12:28.236
- [Shawn] Okay.

01:12:28.236 --> 01:12:30.123
I already have 22.

01:12:30.123 --> 01:12:31.237
- What's that?

01:12:31.237 --> 01:12:33.491
- [Shawn] I started my
vlog, like, 22 episodes,

01:12:33.491 --> 01:12:36.991
but I will start 15 interviews after that,

01:12:37.921 --> 01:12:38.990
and you'll be my 16th?

01:12:38.990 --> 01:12:40.443
- You've done 22 vlog episodes.

01:12:40.443 --> 01:12:41.307
- [Shawn] Vlogs.

01:12:41.307 --> 01:12:42.609
- But if I was listening carefully,

01:12:42.609 --> 01:12:44.706
you asked me to be a
guest on your new podcast.

01:12:44.706 --> 01:12:46.273
- [Shawn] Right, okay, got it.

01:12:46.273 --> 01:12:48.624
- So, that, I'll wait 'til I'm the 16th.

01:12:48.624 --> 01:12:50.021
- [Shawn] Got it, thank you very much.

01:12:50.021 --> 01:12:51.438
- You're welcome.

01:12:56.497 --> 01:12:57.637
- Hello?
- Hello.

01:12:57.637 --> 01:12:59.909
- [Terrance] Yeah, hi,
Gary, my name is Terrance,

01:12:59.909 --> 01:13:01.518
and I'm 20 this year.

01:13:01.518 --> 01:13:03.445
So, just one question for you,

01:13:03.445 --> 01:13:06.296
I've been listening to
you for about a year now,

01:13:06.296 --> 01:13:08.911
and I'm just trying to figure out,

01:13:08.911 --> 01:13:10.902
as a 20 year old without any experience

01:13:10.902 --> 01:13:12.860
in my parents' business,

01:13:12.860 --> 01:13:15.943
I've wanted to build a video, a blog,

01:13:17.064 --> 01:13:19.881
an audio podcast, but I
don't have the experience

01:13:19.881 --> 01:13:21.712
to actually do it.

01:13:21.712 --> 01:13:23.952
So, which answer should I focus on,

01:13:23.952 --> 01:13:26.654
building up the experience in a business,

01:13:26.654 --> 01:13:30.193
or should I go direct to
help market a company?

01:13:30.193 --> 01:13:34.866
- Well, listen, if you started
a podcast and a video blog

01:13:34.866 --> 01:13:38.709
about being experienced in the craft,

01:13:38.709 --> 01:13:40.653
that would be bad,

01:13:40.653 --> 01:13:41.486
faking it.

01:13:42.489 --> 01:13:45.108
But if your podcast was about

01:13:45.108 --> 01:13:48.772
the experience of learning the craft,

01:13:48.772 --> 01:13:52.978
you'd probably have a lot of
20 year olds following you.

01:13:52.978 --> 01:13:56.656
So, I don't think it's about
getting the experience,

01:13:56.656 --> 01:13:59.104
when I talk about I built
a business for 15 years

01:13:59.104 --> 01:14:01.868
before I came out, right?

01:14:01.868 --> 01:14:05.622
I say that because that's what happened,

01:14:05.622 --> 01:14:07.452
but I have a funny feeling
if the internet was around

01:14:07.452 --> 01:14:09.276
when I was a kid, like this,

01:14:09.276 --> 01:14:12.648
I might have started documenting
my journey right away.

01:14:12.648 --> 01:14:14.669
I just wouldn't be walking around

01:14:14.669 --> 01:14:17.648
like I was a business building guy,

01:14:17.648 --> 01:14:19.479
I would be talking about being a young,

01:14:19.479 --> 01:14:23.321
ambitious guy who used
to sell baseball cards

01:14:23.321 --> 01:14:25.681
and now I'm about to do it for wine,

01:14:25.681 --> 01:14:27.928
and I would take people
along with my journey,

01:14:27.928 --> 01:14:29.911
that's my biggest problem with people

01:14:29.911 --> 01:14:33.314
that don't have experience, they're lying.

01:14:33.314 --> 01:14:35.198
They're lying that
they're business experts,

01:14:35.198 --> 01:14:39.198
or my favorite, you're a
20 year old life coach.

01:14:40.129 --> 01:14:43.008
'Cause, you know, you've lived life.

01:14:43.008 --> 01:14:46.318
So, to me, I think you
can start the podcast

01:14:46.318 --> 01:14:50.137
and the video blog, I
mean, I wish I did that,

01:14:50.137 --> 01:14:53.970
because I, there was, I
probably cried, cried,

01:14:55.494 --> 01:14:59.874
50 times in the first 10 years
that I worked with my dad,

01:14:59.874 --> 01:15:02.592
'cause they were very painful fights.

01:15:02.592 --> 01:15:04.504
And that would have
been incredible content

01:15:04.504 --> 01:15:06.126
that I wish you guys could watch

01:15:06.126 --> 01:15:09.348
if you're in a family business,
because it turned out okay,

01:15:09.348 --> 01:15:10.670
and it would have been really cool

01:15:10.670 --> 01:15:12.942
to see how that happened and why,

01:15:12.942 --> 01:15:16.268
and how I was able to
give more than I took,

01:15:16.268 --> 01:15:18.494
and how I loved my dad
more than the money,

01:15:18.494 --> 01:15:20.705
and how I thought about what I could do

01:15:20.705 --> 01:15:24.894
in my 30s and 40s and it's
okay to lose in my 20s,

01:15:24.894 --> 01:15:26.675
but I wouldn't have walked around and said

01:15:26.675 --> 01:15:30.842
I was a marketing genius because
I thought I was gonna be.

01:15:33.492 --> 01:15:34.967
- [Terrance] Yeah.

01:15:34.967 --> 01:15:39.717
So, start documenting my journey
to becoming a businessman?

